  "case": "PostgreSQL text[] XLSX re-import through LibreOffice Calc",
  "test": "array_contract::value_contract_text_array_file_exports_preserve_text_and_escape_markup",
  "engine": "PostgreSQL Docker integration fixture",
  "contract": [
    "Native pg_typeof, array_to_json and array_send oracles check text[] result and parameter round-trip; the fixture includes literal NULL, SQL NULL, empty text, comma, quote, backslash, Unicode and hostile markup.",
    "The text[] value is exported to XLSX as a shared string; the native test checks the expected array text and escaped markup and refuses formulas.",
    "LibreOffice Calc 26.8.0.3 in the pinned Debian image opens XLSX and saves ODS, then reopens ODS and saves XLSX.",
    "A standard-library ZIP/XML checker confirms the exact 84-character text is unchanged in all three artifacts, cell kinds remain string, and no formulas appear."
  ],
  "application": {
    "name": "LibreOffice Calc",
    "version": "26.8.0.3 680(Build:3)",
